[center][size=6][b]HEEL OF ACHILLES[/b][/size]
[i]One cut. They never stand up again.[/i][/center]

Get behind them, slash the back of the heel, and they go down for good. No more trading blows with a tank: find the one spot that matters and end the fight with skill instead of force.

[center][img]{{GIF_CUT}}[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]How it plays[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The cut.[/b] Slash or stab the back of the heel, from behind or the side. Blunt hits and hits from the front do nothing. Swords, thrown daggers and spells all work.
[*][b]The fall.[/b] They drop and never get up. Each enemy rolls its own fate: most sit down and drag themselves after you, some fall onto their knees and fight on, a few just lie there.
[*][b]Still dangerous.[/b] Downed enemies scream, crawl toward you and swing from the ground. Not all of them, though. Good luck guessing which.
[*][b]Bleeding out.[/b] The cut bleeds. They get slower, quieter, start gasping and die after about 45 seconds. Or you end it sooner.
[/list]

[center][img]{{GIF_FATES}}[/img]
[img]{{GIF_HUNT}}[/img]
[img]{{GIF_KNEEL}}[/img]
[img]{{GIF_BLEED}}[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]Your rules[/b][/size]
Everything has a toggle or a slider in the in-game Mod Menu: heel zone size, hit angle, how many enemies kneel, lie flat or fight back, crawl speed, bleed-out time, screams, blood. Changes apply live.

[size=4][b]DMCS[/b][/size]
Running [b]Dark Messiah Combat Systems[/b]? Heel cuts and executions of crippled enemies fill your Adrenaline meter. Fully optional: without DMCS the mod runs on its own, load order does not matter.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Blade & Sorcery 1.3.2 (PC).
[*]Install with Vortex, or copy the [b]AchillesTendon[/b] folder into [i]BladeAndSorcery_Data/StreamingAssets/Mods/[/i].
[*]After an update, press the reset button on the mod's page in the Mod Menu.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Realistic Deaths[/b] also makes enemies crawl and bleed. Both on the same enemy will most likely double the bleeding and fight over the body. Not tested.
[*]Only your hits count. Enemies cutting each other's heels, or yours, do nothing.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Why the heel?[/b][/size]
[b]Achilles[/b] was dipped in the river Styx as a baby and became invulnerable, except for the heel his mother held him by. An arrow from Paris found it.
[b]Krishna[/b] was granted a body no weapon could pierce, except his feet. A hunter took his foot for a deer and loosed an arrow.
Two heroes, one weak point. Now it is your enemies' turn.

[size=4][b]Feedback[/b][/size]
Found a bug or a pose that looks off? Post in the comments with what you did and, if you can, your Player.log. Happy hunting.
